{"tool_name":"cryodrgn","contents":["oeb","bioschemas","biotools"],"fetched_metadata":{"biotools":{"id":"cryodrgn","home":"https://github.com/zhonge/cryodrgn","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"CryoDRGN is a neural network based algorithm for heterogeneous cryo-EM reconstruction.","addition_date":"2021-03-19T08:56:41Z","last_update_date":"2024-11-24T20:26:53.814873Z","tool_type":["Command-line tool"],"biotools_curie":"biotools:cryodrgn","credit":[{"name":"Bonnie Berger","typeEntity":"Person"},{"name":"Joseph H. Davis","typeEntity":"Person"}],"edit_permission":{"type":"private"},"function":[{"operation":[{"term":"Classification","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2990"},{"term":"Clustering","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3432"},{"term":"Principal component visualisation","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_2939"},{"term":"Simulation analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_0244"},{"term":"Single particle analysis","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3457"},{"term":"Trajectory visualization","uri":"http://edamontology.org/operation_3890"}]}],"name":"cryoDRGN","owner":"Kigaard","publication":[{"doi":"10.1038/s41592-020-01049-4","metadata":{"abstract":"Cryo-electron microscopy (cryo-EM) single-particle analysis has proven powerful in determining the structures of rigid macromolecules. However, many imaged protein complexes exhibit conformational and compositional heterogeneity that poses a major challenge to existing three-dimensional reconstruction methods. Here, we present cryoDRGN, an algorithm that leverages the representation power of deep neural networks to directly reconstruct continuous distributions of 3D density maps and map per-particle heterogeneity of single-particle cryo-EM datasets. Using cryoDRGN, we uncovered residual heterogeneity in high-resolution datasets of the 80S ribosome and the RAG complex, revealed a new structural state of the assembling 50S ribosome, and visualized large-scale continuous motions of a spliceosome complex. CryoDRGN contains interactive tools to visualize a dataset\u2019s distribution of per-particle variability, generate density maps for exploratory analysis, extract particle subsets for use with other tools and generate trajectories to visualize molecular motions. CryoDRGN is open-source software freely available at http://cryodrgn.csail.mit.edu.","authors":[{"name":"Bepler T."},{"name":"Berger B."},{"name":"Davis J.H."},{"name":"Zhong E.D."}],"citationCount":285,"date":"2021-02-01T00:00:00Z","journal":"Nature Methods","title":"CryoDRGN: reconstruction of heterogeneous cryo-EM structures using neural networks"},"pmcid":"PMC8183613","pmid":"33542510"}],"topic":[{"term":"Electron microscopy","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0611"},{"term":"Imaging","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3382"},{"term":"Machine learning","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_3474"},{"term":"Molecular dynamics","uri":"http://edamontology.org/topic_0176"}]},"bioschemas":{"name":"cryoDRGN","home":"https://bio.tools/cryodrgn","license":"GPL-3.0","summary":"CryoDRGN is a neural network based algorithm for heterogeneous cryo-EM reconstruction.","tool_type":"sc:SoftwareApplication"},"oeb":{"metrics":[{"@id":"https://openebench.bsc.es/monitor/metrics/biotools:cryodrgn/cmd/github.com","@license":"https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/","@nmsp":"biotools","@type":"metrics","deprecated":true,"distribution":{"binaries":{"freeness":null,"registration":null},"packages":null,"source_packages":false,"sourcecode":{"free":null,"interpreted":true,"license":null,"public":true,"readme":false,"repository":{"anonymous":null,"online":null}}},"project":{"build":{},"deployment":{},"license":{"open_source":true,"osi":true},"publications":[{"entries":[{"cit_count":342,"citations":[{"count":25,"year":"2021"},{"count":51,"year":"2022"},{"count":55,"year":"2023"},{"count":58,"year":"2026"},{"count":75,"year":"2025"},{"count":78,"year":"2024"}],"doi":"10.1038/s41592-020-01049-4","pmcid":"PMC8183613"